{
  "name": "Wall of Force",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>An Invisible wall of force springs into existence at a point you choose within range. The wall appears in any orientation you choose, as a horizontal or vertical barrier or at an angle. It can be free floating or resting on a solid surface. You can form it into a hemispherical dome or a globe with a radius of up to 10 feet, or you can shape a flat surface made up of ten 10-foot-by-10-foot panels. Each panel must be contiguous with another panel. In any form, the wall is 1/4 inch thick and lasts for the duration. If the wall cuts through a creature's space when it appears, the creature is pushed to one side of the wall (you choose which side).</p><p>Nothing can physically pass through the wall. It is immune to all damage and can't be dispelled by <em>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDispelMagi]{Dispel Magic}.</em> A <em>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDisintegra]{Disintegrate}</em> spell destroys the wall instantly, however. The wall also extends into the Ethereal Plane and blocks ethereal travel through the wall.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
